## Timing-replication contract

The new rules are frozen before output:

- one attempt is a complete five-profile campaign over N=96, 192, 256, 320, and 384;
- each profile retains one warm-up pair and all seven alternating-order measured pairs;
- authority requires 3 passing campaigns within at most 5 complete attempts;
- failed attempts and every raw pair remain durable;
- no pair or profile may be selectively excluded;
- any host-quality violation rejects the **whole campaign** only;
- predeclared gates cover source/toolchain/binary identity, host fingerprint, affinity/thread environment, CPU idle/steal, swap, thermal counters, finite positive wall/Gamma values, exact proposed-interval denominators, arm spans, and order sensitivity;
- gate decisions are independent of whether the shadow/R ratio is favorable.

